# * the VM (~/.env). Fill values, then put the contents into
# * cloud-init/user-data.example.yml (write_files block). NEVER commit the
# * filled file.
# * Docs: docs/user-edits.md
# ****************************************************************************
# Template for the .env file that cloud-init injects into the VM (~/.env).
# Copy and fill values, then put the contents in cloud-init/user-data
# (write_files block). NEVER commit the filled file.
#
# The VM is disposable and runs with short-lived tokens. If these leak, the
# blast radius is intentionally small. Prefer temporary/short-expiry keys.
#
# ISSUE A SEPARATE, SHORT-LIVED KEY PER AGENT — one for opencode, one for
# codex, one for goose — and only for providers you actually enable in
# ansible/vars/ai-tools.list. A separate key per agent means you can revoke a
# single one (e.g. a leaked VM) without rotating the others, and cap expiry
# to days, not years.
#
# Provider credentials for AI agents, for example:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENCODE_MODEL=your-model
